{
  "info": {
    "name": "Oxide API",
    "description": "Text and markdown extraction from PDF, Office (DOCX/XLSX/PPTX/DOC/XLS/PPT), OpenDocument (ODT/ODS/ODP) and image files (PNG/JPEG/TIFF/WebP/GIF/BMP/JP2/PNM/TGA), with OCR (en, hi, ar) for scanned PDFs and images. The file type is detected from the content, so every request in `extract` takes any of them.\n\nAuth: `OXIDE_API_API_KEY` as Bearer token on all `POST /v1/*`. Set the `apiKey` collection/environment variable. Ops endpoints (`GET /healthz`, `/readyz`, `/version`, `/metrics`, `/openapi.json`, `/openapi.yaml`, `/docs`) are unauthenticated.\n\nFolders: `extract` (every endpoint, any file), `images (OCR)` and `opendocument` (format-specific examples), `ops`.\n\nImport this file + `oxide-api.postman_environment.json` into Postman, set `apiKey` to your key, pick a file for the `file` form-data key on multipart requests. The file sources point at the repo's test fixtures: set Postman's working directory to the repo root (Settings → General → Working directory) to send them as-is, or pick your own file.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{apiKey}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": "CHANGE-ME-TO-OXIDE_API_API_KEY",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "extract",
      "description": "Authenticated. Bearer `{{apiKey}}` (= `OXIDE_API_API_KEY`) is inherited from the collection.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/extract/text (multipart)",
          "request": {
            "description": "Plain text from any supported file. Office and OpenDocument: the document's text. PDF: per-page native text, with OCR for pages that need it. Images: OCR text per page. Multipart is preferred for large files.\n\nOptional query params: `pages=1-3,5`, `ocr=auto|force|off`, `lang=auto|en|hi|ar` (PDFs and images), `format=pdf|docx|xlsx|pptx|doc|xls|ppt|odt|ods|odp|png|jpeg|tiff|webp|gif|bmp|jp2|pnm|tga`, `filename=report.pdf`, `clean=true|false` (any: collapse extra spaces/tabs and blank lines).",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/extract/text",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "extract", "text"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "description": "Pick any supported file: PDF, DOCX / XLSX / PPTX / DOC / XLS / PPT, ODT / ODS / ODP, or an image (PNG / JPEG / TIFF / WebP / GIF / BMP / JP2 / PNM / TGA).",
                  "src": ""
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 with extracted text\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var j = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(j.text).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.char_count).to.be.above(0);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/extract/text (JSON base64)",
          "request": {
            "description": "Same endpoint via JSON. Handy for n8n / Dify / Zapier. Replace FILE_BASE64 with `base64 < file | tr -d '\\n'`. The 32 MiB limit counts the base64 text. `format` is only a hint (the content decides); drop it or set it to the file's type, e.g. `ods` or `png`.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/extract/text",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "extract", "text"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"file_base64\": \"FILE_BASE64\",\n  \"format\": \"pdf\",\n  \"pages\": \"1-3\",\n  \"ocr\": \"auto\",\n  \"lang\": \"auto\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 with extracted text\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var j = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(j.text).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/extract/text (raw body, text/plain)",
          "request": {
            "description": "Raw bytes as body + `Accept: text/plain` returns raw text (metadata in `X-Oxide-*` headers, e.g. `X-Oxide-Kind: image`, `X-Oxide-Ocr-Status`). Example query: `?pages=2`. In Postman: Body -> Binary -> pick file.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "text/plain"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/extract/text?pages=1-3",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "extract", "text"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "pages",
                  "value": "1-3",
                  "description": "PDFs and images (TIFF pages). 1-based pages and ranges, e.g. 1-3,5."
                },
                {
                  "key": "ocr",
                  "value": "auto",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "PDFs and images: auto | force | off. Images are always OCR'd unless off."
                },
                {
                  "key": "lang",
                  "value": "auto",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "PDFs and images: auto | en | hi | ar"
                }
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "file",
              "file": {
                "src": ""
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 text/plain\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\")).to.include(\"text/plain\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/extract/markdown (multipart)",
          "request": {
            "description": "Office and OpenDocument: headings, lists, tables (one table per sheet, one section per slide). PDF: per-page markdown with heading detection. Images: OCR lines and paragraphs. Extra param vs text: `detect_headings=true|false` (PDF only), `clean=true|false` (any).",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/extract/markdown",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "extract", "markdown"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "description": "Pick any supported file: PDF, DOCX / XLSX / PPTX / DOC / XLS / PPT, ODT / ODS / ODP, or an image (PNG / JPEG / TIFF / WebP / GIF / BMP / JP2 / PNM / TGA).",
                  "src": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "detect_headings",
                  "value": "true",
                  "type": "text",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "PDF markdown only."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 with markdown\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().text).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/extract/markdown (raw body, text/markdown)",
          "request": {
            "description": "Raw bytes + `Accept: text/markdown` returns raw markdown. In Postman: Body -> Binary -> pick file.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "text/markdown"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/extract/markdown",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "extract", "markdown"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "file",
              "file": {
                "src": ""
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 text/markdown\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\")).to.include(\"text/markdown\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/info (multipart)",
          "request": {
            "description": "Format, metadata and structure without extracting text. Office and OpenDocument: metadata, sheet names and dimensions, slide count, section count. PDF: version, page count, encryption, page geometry. Images: page count and pixel dimensions, read from the headers (nothing is decoded).",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/info",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "info"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "description": "Pick any supported file: PDF, DOCX / XLSX / PPTX / DOC / XLS / PPT, ODT / ODS / ODP, or an image (PNG / JPEG / TIFF / WebP / GIF / BMP / JP2 / PNM / TGA).",
                  "src": ""
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 with info\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var j = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(j.format).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.format_source).to.be.oneOf([\"sniff\", \"param\", \"filename\"]);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "images (OCR)",
      "description": "Images go straight to OCR (en, hi, ar): PNG, JPEG, TIFF (one page per TIFF page, CCITT fax TIFFs included), WebP, GIF (first frame), BMP, JPEG 2000, PNM, TGA. EXIF orientation is applied, so a sideways phone photo reads correctly, and transparent backgrounds are composited onto white. The response has the PDF shape with `kind: image`; every page's `ocr.reasons` entry is `image`.\n\nLimits: 64 megapixels per page (`OXIDE_API_MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS`, else `422 image-too-large`), 2000 TIFF pages. HEIC/HEIF (iPhone camera files), AVIF and JPEG XL are rejected with a `422 unsupported-format` that names the format: convert them to JPEG or PNG first.\n\nThe file sources point at the repo's test fixtures: set Postman's working directory to the repo root (Settings → General → Working directory) to send them as-is, or pick your own file.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/extract/text — image (multipart)",
          "request": {
            "description": "OCR text of an image. `lang=auto` probes the first page's text with every recognizer; set `lang` when you know the language. TGA has no signature: the uploaded filename (`.tga`) or `format=tga` identifies it.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/extract/text",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "extract", "text"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "description": "An image: PNG, JPEG, TIFF, WebP, GIF, BMP, JP2, PNM or TGA. The fixture is an English invoice scan.",
                  "src": "tests/fixtures/scan_en.png"
                },
                {
                  "key": "lang",
                  "value": "auto",
                  "type": "text",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "auto | en | hi | ar"
                },
                {
                  "key": "ocr",
                  "value": "off",
                  "type": "text",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "off returns no text; the image is still validated."
                },
                {
                  "key": "format",
                  "value": "tga",
                  "type": "text",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Only needed for a TGA uploaded without a .tga filename."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200, image OCR'd\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var j = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(j.kind).to.eql(\"image\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.ocr.status).to.be.oneOf([\"ocr\", \"off\", \"unavailable\"]);",
                  "    pm.expect(j.text).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.page_count).to.be.at.least(1);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/extract/text — sideways phone photo (EXIF)",
          "request": {
            "description": "The fixture's pixels are stored rotated 90° with EXIF Orientation 6, like a photo taken with the phone held sideways. The service rotates it upright before OCR.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/extract/text",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "extract", "text"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "description": "A JPEG photo; the fixture carries EXIF Orientation 6.",
                  "src": "tests/fixtures/scan_en_exif.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200, photo OCR'd upright\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var j = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(j.kind).to.eql(\"image\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.ocr.status).to.be.oneOf([\"ocr\", \"off\", \"unavailable\"]);",
                  "    pm.expect(j.text).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.format).to.eql(\"jpeg\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/extract/text — multi-page TIFF, page 2 (raw body)",
          "request": {
            "description": "A multi-page TIFF is one page per TIFF page; `pages` selects them like PDF pages (omit it for all). The fixture is a two-page CCITT Group 4 fax TIFF. In Postman: Body -> Binary -> pick file.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/extract/text?pages=2",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "extract", "text"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "pages",
                  "value": "2",
                  "description": "1-based TIFF pages, e.g. 1-3,5"
                }
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "file",
              "file": {
                "src": "tests/fixtures/scan_pages.tif"
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200, only page 2\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var j = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(j.kind).to.eql(\"image\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.ocr.status).to.be.oneOf([\"ocr\", \"off\", \"unavailable\"]);",
                  "    pm.expect(j.text).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.page_count).to.be.at.least(2);",
                  "    pm.expect(j.pages_extracted).to.eql([2]);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
